## ⚠️ DO NOT TRUNCATE PERSISTENT MEMORY

The memory hierarchy is load-bearing. Skipping it means starting dumber than the last session.

- **Read PERSISTENT.md in full** at session start. Don't skim.
- **Query the KB** when the topic is non-trivial. `kb entity <slug>`, `kb search <term>`, `kb pending-reviews` are cheap.
- **Don't fatten this file (MEMORY.md).** It truncates past 200 lines. Keep it as index + critical ops safety only. New context goes to PERSISTENT.md or KB.
- **"I don't have time to read all that" is the wrong instinct.** The 1M context window exists so you can. Read it.

